ion\\\"\"\nresponse-format-4-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-action\nresponse-format-4-content ::= \"\\\"\" char+ \"\\\"\"\nresponse-format-4-content-kv ::= \"\\\"content\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-content\nresponse-format-5 ::= \"{\" space response-format-5-action-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-5-action ::= \"\\\"run_check\\\"\"\nresponse-format-5-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-5-action\nresponse-format-6 ::= \"{\" space response-format-6-action-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-6-action ::= \"\\\"submit\\\"\"\nresponse-format-6-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-6-action\nroot ::= \"<|im_start|>assistant\\n\" (\"<think>\" space until-5 (\"</think>\" | ))? space response-format\nspace ::= | \" \" | \"\\n\"{1,2} [ \\t]{0,20}\nuntil-5 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<] until-5\nuntil-5-01 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [/] until-5-02 | [t] until-5-09 | [^/<t] until-5\nuntil-5-02 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [t] until-5-03 | [^<t] until-5\nuntil-5-03 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [h] until-5-04 | [^<h] until-5\nuntil-5-04 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [i] until-5-05 | [^<i] until-5\nuntil-5-05 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [n] until-5-06 | [^<n] until-5\nuntil-5-06 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [k] until-5-07 | [^<k] until-5\nuntil-5-07 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\nuntil-5-09 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-10 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-10 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-11 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-11 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-12 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-12 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [_] until-5-13 | [^<_] until-5\nuntil-5-13 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [c] until-5-14 | [^<c] until-5\nuntil-5-14 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [a] until-5-15 | [^<a] until-5\nuntil-5-15 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-16 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-16 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-17 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-17 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\n","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"next_token":[{"has_next_token":false,"has_new_line":false,"n_remain":-1,"n_decoded":0}],"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# System contract\n\nYou are the task actor in a bounded exact-world experiment. Return exactly one\ndeclared JSON action and no prose. Exact sources, candidate files, actions,\neffects, checks, and history are externally custodied. Receipts identify exact\nrecoverable results but do not contain their semantic substance.\n\nUse only evidence that has crossed your model boundary. A semantic integration\nledger is lossy and non-authoritative. A check is current only for the exact\ncomposite candidate hash it evaluated. Submission is a proposal for external\ncandidate-bound adjudication, not proof that migration or closure is ready.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Task: Northstar migration architecture decision package\n\nNorthstar is moving a multi-region event-ingestion service from LegacyQueue to\nStreamCore. Produce two exact deliverables from the source catalog:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`\n\nThe package must decide a safe, source-grounded ninety-day migration route. It\nmust reconcile service objectives, event identity, schema compatibility,\nregional residency, incident history, capacity, vendor limits, rollout gates,\nverification, rollback, and readiness. Do not merely summarize sources.\n\n## Evidence-ledger contract\n\nThe ledger must begin with `# Evidence Integration Ledger` and contain entries\nfor `R01` through `R12`. Each entry must state a current disposition, cite exact\nobserved sources as `[SNN]`, preserve conflicts and qualifications, and identify\nunresolved evidence or blockers. A model-authored ledger is lossy and is never\nreadiness authority.\n\n## Decision-document contract\n\nThe decision must begin with `# Northstar Migration Architecture Decision` and\nuse exactly these level-two headings, in this order:\n\n1. `## Decision and scope`\n2. `## Protocol, topology, and authority`\n3. `## Delivery, identity, and schema safety`\n4. `## Residency, continuity, and failure response`\n5. `## Capacity, observability, and reconciliation`\n6. `## Ninety-day rollout and rollback plan`\n7. `## Verification, readiness, and governance`\n8. `## Risks, uncertainties, and falsifiers`\n\nThe decision must be 1,500–2,100 words excluding exact `[SNN]` citations, cite\nat least ten distinct source IDs, and cite `S01`, `S03`, `S04`, `S06`, `S07`,\n`S08`, `S10`, `S11`, `S12`, and `S14`.\n\nThe complete package must substantively resolve these requirements:\n\n- `R01`: authoritative topology, regional scope, and authority transitions;\n- `R02`: service objectives, including tenant-local and regional tail gates;\n- `R03`: producer_id:event_id identity, acknowledgement, at-least-once effects,\n  and a deduplication horizon covering the observed 31-hour retry;\n- `R04`: schema-v3 compatibility and the boundary between safe rollback and\n  forward-fix;\n- `R05`: staged cohort rollout, dwell, hold, and advancement gates;\n- `R06`: EU payload residency and the override of generic global failover;\n- `R07`: continuity sized against the observed vendor outage rather than the\n  contractual target alone;\n- `R08`: candidate-bound telemetry and full tenant-hour reconciliation;\n- `R09`: us-west capacity sequencing, spool expansion, and retirement of\n  migration-only cost;\n- `R10`: security, retention, access, audit, and deletion controls;\n- `R11`: a concrete ninety-day sequence with owners, effects, checks, repair,\n  and recheck;\n- `R12`: readiness authority, blocking evidence, uncertainties, and explicit\n  falsifiers.\n\nDo not claim exactly-once delivery, lossless schema-v3 failback through\nLegacyQueue, unrestricted EU-to-US failover, guaranteed four-hour vendor\nrecovery, or readiness established by a stale or fleet-average-only check.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Ordinary actor actions\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object and no surrounding prose.\n\n- `{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":120}`\n- `{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":120},{\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":120}]}`\n- `{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"# Evidence Integration Ledger\\n...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"heading\":\"Decision and scope\",\"body\":\"...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"replace_decision\",\"content\":\"# Northstar Migration Architecture Decision\\n...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"run_check\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"submit\"}`\n\nOne source range is at most 240 lines. A batch contains at most three\nnon-overlapping ranges, 480 total lines, and 40,000 exact source bytes. A\nsection upsert changes one declared level-two section while preserving the\nother exact sections. Checks bind to the current composite candidate hash.\n\n\n# Exact source catalog\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":95,\"sha256\":\"d52a4de79cc8eefc56a7ee973e39ea74ff9279bd69fa2f88d5367c91d77b4a6b\",\"size_bytes\":7012,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"title\":\"Northstar topology and migration target\"},{\"line_count\":89,\"sha256\":\"09a092be1b2271e85f5409d942f3aeaf99ac6a34e2d326414eb74da99c24bab1\",\"size_bytes\":5739,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"title\":\"Northstar service objectives and traffic evidence\"},{\"line_count\":201,\"sha256\":\"a9fc86604868d446c8c4ec33391b083b9dcad930f595591719b54f7d1a0e8c77\",\"size_bytes\":13257,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"title\":\"Delivery, acknowledgement, and idempotency contract\"},{\"line_count\":89,\"sha256\":\"766c7ac526bce24096b07dad7db41e873f871ef90adc6457c7a7f5a29d02c6c7\",\"size_bytes\":5441,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"title\":\"Schema compatibility and rollback boundaries\"},{\"line_count\":39,\"sha256\":\"7ee48b0e33e065bccb6ef34320162a38af6a807189dda0c2891d851466940c9d\",\"size_bytes\":3639,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"title\":\"Rollout, hold, and rollback policy\"},{\"line_count\":226,\"sha256\":\"eb036514fa12cfe37eb7f51cdea5e91c9f4532b5a87163ee36ea56aef8bd0542\",\"size_bytes\":17344,\"source_id\":\"S06\",\"title\":\"Incident E-17: delayed replay and duplicate storm\"},{\"line_count\":226,\"sha256\":\"699b970f35b6cb56fcabb56185367349923fedd68cb9b138c8d66064c69294ad\",\"size_bytes\":17781,\"source_id\":\"S07\",\"title\":\"Incident E-23: EU residency failover violation\"},{\"line_count\":226,\"sha256\":\"186e76184a557b0be2193cb05b2a19cb1748eb8820219476408ff4a9fd34ca87\",\"size_bytes\":17387,\"source_id\":\"S08\",\"title\":\"Incident E-31: dependency outage beyond SLA\"},{\"line_count\":76,\"sha256\":\"b614f068d046ffa3b7387a65df23afbfcb66587c96b05e41096dd60d0505698a\",\"size_bytes\":3912,\"source_id\":\"S09\",\"title\":\"Tail-latency and cohort telemetry review\"},{\"line_count\":256,\"sha256\":\"70347d29366f7ca1a8306c281eb36e0b441a08c6eeb75edf4a4f5807cb4b8348\",\"size_bytes\":15956,\"source_id\":\"S10\",\"title\":\"Shadow reconciliation and data-integrity audit\"},{\"line_count\":160,\"sha256\":\"a8b8ae5d65a200926f29de521df2f046e13fffe954b3b028820bef47e7b349f6\",\"size_bytes\":9817,\"source_id\":\"S11\",\"title\":\"Security, privacy, retention, and audit controls\"},{\"line_count\":79,\"sha256\":\"6e470856b40ef482af53286c8eeb98801ae26b844c884bc9450053566262b1a2\",\"size_bytes\":4107,\"source_id\":\"S12\",\"title\":\"Capacity, spool, and migration cost model\"},{\"line_count\":135,\"sha256\":\"4b3f1e60d98c3312fabaaf55585a6a6996bfa8601b01c9bf5583db9fc041d967\",\"size_by